    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19472" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gĕnŭa</span></b> , ae,
			f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a celebrated seaport town of Liguria</i>, <i>a
				famous market for timber</i>, now <i>Genoa</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Mel.
				2, 4, 9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 5, 7, § 48</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 28,
			46</span></i>; <i><span class="en">30, 1
			al.</span></i>; <i>its inhabitants</i> are called
			‡ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gĕnŭātes</span></b>  and
			‡ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gĕnŭenses</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Inscr.
					Orell. 3121</span></i> (of the year A. U. C. 637, B. C.
			117); v. also Genava.</div>
